title: Add `provider_name()` to `BlockNumberProvider` trait
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    Adds a `provider_name()` method to the `BlockNumberProvider` trait that returns a
    human-readable name identifying the block number source. This allows application
    developers to determine which block number provider a pallet is configured with
    (e.g. local system block number vs relay chain block number). The default
    implementation uses `core::any::type_name`. `frame_system::Pallet` returns "System"
    and `RelaychainDataProvider` returns "RelaychainDataProvider".

crates:
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: frame-system
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: patch
